  "summary": "This one-page English newspaper clipping reports the estimated cost of India’s Union Ministers and Deputy Ministers. It states that the revised estimate for 1969–70 was Rs 42,66,399, compared with Rs 43,79,907 in 1968–69, and gives Rs 34,60,491 as the expenditure for 1967–68 on salaries, allowances, touring, and the maintenance of government accommodation. The clipping notes that there were 55 Central Ministers and Deputy Ministers.\n\nThe figures are attributed partly to PTI and partly to a statement laid before the Rajya Sabha by Deputy Home Minister K. S. Ramaswamy. The lower portion reports additional expenditure relating to 275 other office-holders, but the text is damaged and difficult to read. The clipping has no visible newspaper masthead, byline, or date; its bottom section is also affected by a horizontal tear.",
